timeline
    title EU AI Act Enforcement Timeline (Regulation 2024/1689, updated with Digital Omnibus on AI provisional agreement of 7 May 2026)
    section 2024
        1 Aug 2024  : Published in Official Journal of the EU
                    : Act enters into force (12 Jul 2024)
    section 2025
        2 Feb 2025  : ✅ Prohibited AI practices apply (Art. 5)
                   : ✅ AI literacy obligations (Art. 4)
                   : Fines up to €35M / 7% turnover for prohibited practices
        2 Aug 2025  : ✅ GPAI model obligations apply (Art. 53–55)
                   : ✅ GPAI Code of Practice published (10 Jul 2025)
                   : ✅ Governance & penalties chapters apply
        6 Oct 2025  : ✅ AI Liability Directive (AILD) proposal formally withdrawn (OJ notice)
        10 Oct 2025 : ✅ Italy Legge 132/2025 enters into force (first national AI law in the EU)
    section 2026
        2 Feb 2026  : ✅ Commission guidelines on high-risk classification (Art. 6)
        20 Jan 2026 : ✅ EDPB-EDPS Joint Opinion 1/2026 on the Digital Omnibus on AI
        7 May 2026  : ✅ Digital Omnibus on AI: Council and Parliament provisional agreement
                   : 9th Article 5 prohibition added (non-consensual intimate content & CSAM)
        2 Aug 2026  : Pre-Omnibus binding date for high-risk Annex III, Art. 50, Art. 57 sandboxes
                   : (until OJ publication of the Omnibus)
        2 Dec 2026  : Art. 50 transparency obligations apply (Omnibus, 3-month grace from OJ)
                   : AI-generated content watermarking requirements
        9 Dec 2026  : Revised Product Liability Directive transposition deadline
    section 2027
        2 Aug 2027  : National AI regulatory sandboxes operational (Omnibus, postponed by 1 year)
                   : Legacy GPAI models must comply
        2 Dec 2027  : High-risk AI obligations apply (Annex III) (Omnibus)
                   : Full Title III requirements for new high-risk systems
                   : Full penalty regime active
    section 2028
        2 Aug 2028  : High-risk AI in regulated products (Art. 6.1) (Omnibus)
                   : Medical devices, machinery, vehicles, etc.
    section 2030
        2 Aug 2030  : Legacy public sector AI systems must comply
        31 Dec 2030 : Large-scale IT system AI components must comply
